{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if from sixty years old and upward.</b> From where do we know that the sixtieth year and below is included under it? Scripture says, <b>ואם מבן ששים שנה ומעלה אם זכר</b> etc. — this teaches that the sixtieth year and below is included under it. This tells me only about the sixtieth year; the fifth year, the twentieth year — from where? It follows by inference: just as the sixtieth year is obligated, so the fifth year and the twentieth year are obligated; just as the sixtieth year and below is included under it, so too the fifth year and the twentieth year and below are included. That Scripture diminishes the valuation of an old man from what it was when he was a young man, more than it diminishes for a woman — the reason is that a man's trade is according to his strength, heavy labor, and when he is old his strength is spent and he cannot stand up to it. But a woman's way is in light crafts, and when she is old she can still do them to some degree."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:45.966770834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}